WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.290 --> 00:00:04.680
The world's top climate-change denier may
be US President Donald Trump.

00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:09.230
But around the world populists, including
the president of Brazil, are attacking what

00:00:09.230 --> 00:00:15.070
they call the myth of global warming and forcing
environmentalists to defend accepted scientific

00:00:15.070 --> 00:00:18.900
wisdom.

00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:20.230
Germany is no exception.

00:00:20.230 --> 00:00:26.530
Here the far-right populist AfD party argues
that humans don't cause climate change.

00:00:26.530 --> 00:00:31.730
The most important thing is education and
people's common sense.

00:00:31.730 --> 00:00:36.480
Despite relatively constant CO2 levels in
the past 10 years, there have been huge variations

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:37.830
in climate.

00:00:37.830 --> 00:00:45.870
There is no cause and effect between CO2 and
temperatures.

00:00:45.870 --> 00:00:52.050
The AfD wants to reverse Germany's ambitious
Renewable Energy Sources Act, cancel the country's

00:00:52.050 --> 00:00:59.420
planned phase-out of coal power and take it
out of the 2015 Paris Agreement on climate.

00:00:59.420 --> 00:01:03.340
That makes the co-leader of Germany's Green
Party see red.

00:01:03.340 --> 00:01:10.580
The AfD is not only a far-right and sometimes
extremist party that isn't always committed

00:01:10.580 --> 00:01:15.540
to our constitution -- it also doesn't stand
for freedom of research.

00:01:15.540 --> 00:01:20.740
It doesn't acknowledge that on the environment
and in particular climate change we have evidence

00:01:20.740 --> 00:01:23.870
accepted by scientists all over the world.

00:01:23.870 --> 00:01:31.540
Instead it questions science itself."

00:01:31.540 --> 00:01:36.120
The Greens say Germany's mainstream parties
should continue discussing climate protection

00:01:36.120 --> 00:01:39.340
and not get stuck in quarrels with the AfD.

00:01:39.340 --> 00:01:42.620
But that may be easier said than done.

00:01:42.620 --> 00:01:47.680
The AfD and the Greens are vying to become
Germany's second most powerful political party,

00:01:47.680 --> 00:01:54.910
and the climate is an issue where the populists
can take a clear stand against the mainstream.

00:01:54.910 --> 00:02:00.060
Man-made climate change IS a problem for the
vast majority of Bundestag delegates.

00:02:00.060 --> 00:02:04.790
But battles to set the environmental agenda
are raging on the national level in many places

00:02:04.790 --> 00:02:08.610
around the world -- including ecologically
progressive Germany.

